---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/service.css";

const SITE = "https://www.tmdesignengineering.com";
const url = `${SITE}/services/engineering-verification`;
const faqs = [
  ["What's the difference between verification and validation?", "Verification asks \"did we build the design right?\" — does it meet its spec, is it safe, will it survive real use. Validation asks \"did we build the right thing?\" for the user. This service is about verification: proving, with analysis and testing, that a design does what it needs to before you spend money on tooling."],
  ["Do I need a finished design first?", "Ideally you have a design or a detailed concept — CAD, drawings or a working prototype. The more defined it is, the more precisely I can analyse and test it. If it's still taking shape, Concept & MVP Development or a Feasibility Study is usually the better starting point."],
  ["Can you actually run the tests, or just plan them?", "Both. I define what needs proving and how, run the engineering analysis and simulation myself, and coordinate specialist or accredited testing (EMC, safety, environmental, lifecycle) with trusted labs where that's needed — then pull it all together into one report."],
  ["Will this help me pass certification?", "It's designed to. Catching the issues that fail safety and compliance testing before you commit to tooling is far cheaper than discovering them at certification. I can't issue certificates myself, but I get a design into the shape where it's ready to pass."],
  ["How much does it cost?", "It depends on the product and how much needs proving, so I scope and price it after a free intro call — you'll always know the cost before any work begins. A focused Design Review (from £200) is often the right first step."],
];
const jsonld = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "@id": `${url}#service`,
    serviceType: "Engineering verification and testing",
    name: "Engineering Verification",
    description: "Prove a product design works, is safe and is compliant before committing to tooling — engineering analysis, simulation and structured testing, delivered as a verification report.",
    provider: { "@id": `${SITE}/#business` },
    areaServed: ["United Kingdom", "Worldwide"],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Engineering Verification", item: url },
    ],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      name: q,
      acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: a },
    })),
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Engineering Verification & Testing | Thomas McKee"
  description="Prove your product design works, is safe and is compliant before you commit to tooling — engineering analysis, simulation and structured testing, delivered as a verification report you can act on."
  type="website"
  jsonld={jsonld}>
<main>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="svc-hero">
    <div class="wrap svc-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Service · Engineering Verification</span>
        <h1>Know your design works — <em>before you commit to tooling.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Tooling is where a product gets expensive to change. Verification is how you make sure the design is right first: engineering analysis, simulation and structured testing that prove it performs, survives real use and meets its safety and compliance targets — while fixes are still cheap.</p>
        <div class="svc-hero-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#included">See what you get</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="spec" aria-label="Service summary">
        <div class="spec-head"><span>Service Spec</span><span>EV—03</span></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Deliver</div><div class="spec-v">Verification report</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Covers</div><div class="spec-v">Analysis · sim · test</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Timing</div><div class="spec-v">Before tooling</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Price</div><div class="spec-v">Scoped up front</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">You need</div><div class="spec-v">A design or prototype</div></div>
        <div class="spec-note">A focused Design Review (from £200) is often the right first step; larger verification programmes are scoped and fixed-quoted after a free intro call.</div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PAIN -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Who it's for</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">If you're about to spend real money on tooling</h2>
      <div class="pain">
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"The design looks right on screen — but will it actually hold up in the real world?"</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"Is it safe and compliant, or am I about to fail certification and lose months?"</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"Where are the weak points I can't see — and which one becomes a recall?"</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-intro">Verification answers these with evidence, not opinion, before the design is frozen in steel. A problem caught in analysis costs hours; the same problem caught after tooling costs a new tool — and the same problem caught after launch costs your reputation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT YOU GET -->
  <section class="band" id="included">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">What you get</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Evidence your design is ready</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">A clear picture of how the design behaves, where the risks are and what to do about them — written down so you, your team and your suppliers are working from the same facts.</p>
      <div class="deliv">
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">01</div><h3>Design review &amp; risk analysis</h3><p>A structured review of the design against its requirements, with the failure modes identified and ranked so the real risks get attention first.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">02</div><h3>Engineering analysis &amp; simulation</h3><p>Hand calculations and simulation — structural, thermal, fluid or tolerance — to predict how it performs and where it's marginal, before anything is built.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">03</div><h3>Test planning &amp; specialist testing</h3><p>A test plan that proves the things that matter, and coordination of specialist safety, EMC, environmental or lifecycle testing with trusted labs where it's needed.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">04</div><h3>A verification report</h3><p>Findings, evidence and a prioritised list of design changes — a document you can act on and take to suppliers, partners or certification.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROCESS -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">How it works</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">From design to proof</h2>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">1</div><div><h3>Free intro call</h3><p>You tell me the product and where it's headed. I tell you honestly what's worth verifying, and confirm scope and price before anything starts.</p><div class="meta">Free · 30 minutes</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">2</div><div><h3>Review &amp; analysis</h3><p>I work through the design against its requirements, run the calculations and simulation, and map the failure modes — building an honest picture of where it's strong and where it's marginal.</p><div class="meta">Scoped phase</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">3</div><div><h3>Test where it counts</h3><p>We prove the critical claims with the right test — my own, or coordinated with specialist labs for safety, EMC, environmental or lifecycle work.</p><div class="meta">Scoped phase</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">4</div><div><h3>Report &amp; recommendations</h3><p>Everything written up: what was found, the evidence behind it, and a prioritised set of changes — so the design that goes to tooling is one you trust.</p><div class="meta">Deliverable</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SCOPE -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Scope</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Clear on both sides</h2>
      <div class="scope">
        <div class="scard need">
          <h3>What you bring</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><span class="tick">→</span> A design or prototype — CAD, drawings or a working sample. The more defined, the sharper the analysis.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">→</span> What it needs to do, and any standards or targets it has to meet.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">→</span> The decision it's feeding — tooling sign-off, certification, an investor milestone.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="scard">
          <h3>How I work</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> Mechanical, thermal and firmware seen as one system — problems rarely respect the boundaries between them.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> Analysis and testing chosen to answer real questions, not to generate paperwork.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> Happy to work under an NDA from the first conversation.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> Findings explained in plain terms, with the trade-offs made explicit.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-cred">
        <span class="ci"><b>4+ years</b> verifying consumer products at Ooni</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>Thermal, structural &amp; firmware</b> analysis under one roof</span>
        <span class="ci">Safety- and compliance-critical <b>high-temperature</b> work</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Before you book</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (
          <div class="fitem"><div class="fq">{q}</div><div class="fa">{a}</div></div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="band" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta">
        <div class="inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Start here</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Make sure it's right before it's steel</h2>
          <p>Book a free intro call and tell me what's coming up to tooling or certification. We'll work out what's worth verifying and how — and I'll scope and price it before anything begins.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
            <span class="price-tag">Design Reviews from <b>£200</b></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
